cat << 'EOF' > build_error.log
================================================================================
IPON APP DEVELOPMENT LOG - ZIP EXTRACTION TO SUCCESSFUL BUILD TIMELINE
================================================================================

1. SCRIPT EXECUTION ENVIRONMENT ERRORS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Bug Encountered: Cryptic "Required file not found" when executing ./gradlew.
* Root Cause: The gradlew startup script was saved with Windows carriage return
  line endings (CRLF) instead of Linux line endings (LF).
* Fix Applied: Ran 'sed -i "s/\r$//" gradlew' to strip out the Windows hidden
  characters and restore script execution compatibility.

2. DEEP GIT REPOSITORY CORRUPTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Bug Encountered: 'fatal: unknown index entry format' followed by
  'error: non-monotonic index' and 'fatal: pack has bad object'.
* Root Cause: The AI Studio ZIP contained its own hidden .git directory. Direct
  overwriting blended two completely separate Git histories and physically
  corrupted the packed tracking objects beyond manual repair.
* Fix Applied (The Clean Slate): 
  - Nuked the corrupted history folder entirely: 'rm -rf .git'
  - Initialized a brand new, clean local repository: 'git init'
  - Linked the healthy local repo to the remote origin:
    'git remote add origin https://github.com/yannero18/Ipon.git'
  - Safely synchronized histories using a forced push:
    'git push -u origin main --force'

3. GRADLE VERSION MATCHING & DUPLICATE RESOURCES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Bug Encountered: 'Minimum supported Gradle version is 8.9. Current version is 8.7'.
* Root Cause: The Android Gradle Plugin (AGP) version 8.7.0 required a higher 
  Gradle ecosystem environment than what was declared in the properties file.
* Fix Applied: Modified 'gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties' distributionUrl
  to fetch and target Gradle 8.9.

* Bug Encountered: 'Resource and asset merger: Duplicate resources (Theme.Ipon)'.
* Root Cause: The core app theme style layout block was identically duplicated
  across both 'styles.xml' and 'themes.xml'.
* Fix Applied: Backed up the file out of the resources track and blanked out
  'styles.xml' to eliminate the duplicate merger declaration.

4. MISSING ASSETS & KEYSTORES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Bug Encountered: 'File google-services.json is missing. The Google Services
  Plugin cannot function without it.'
* Root Cause: The project configuration required Firebase credentials which were not 
  packaged inside the template.
* Fix Applied: Deactivated line 10 'alias(libs.plugins.google.services)' and 
  commented out lines 75-77 'googleServices { ... }' in 'app/build.gradle.kts'.

* Bug Encountered: 'Keystore file debug.keystore not found for signing config'.
* Root Cause: Wiping the corrupted .git folder also removed the temporary developer 
  signing key requested by the build config.
* Fix Applied: Generated a fresh development signature key using Java's built-in 
  'keytool' engine directly in the workspace root path.

* Warning Encountered: 'sdk.dir property in local.properties file. Problem: Directory does not exist'.
* Root Cause: The local configuration properties contained absolute local machine paths
  instead of matching the cloud virtual machine architecture.
* Fix Applied: Overwrote 'local.properties' to explicitly map the system target to 
  '/home/codespace/android-sdk'.

5. OUT OF MEMORY (OOM) CRASHES & HEADLESS COMPILER BUGS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Bug Encountered: 'Gradle build daemon disappeared unexpectedly' during KSP processing.
* Root Cause 1 (RAM Starvation): Heavy background tasks spiked resource usage past 
  the maximum 4GB memory capacity allocated to the GitHub Codespace instance,
  triggering the Linux kernel OOM (Out-of-Memory) system killer to forcefully abort.
* Root Cause 2 (KSP Headless Bug): Google's KSP compilation plugin version 2.3.5
  contained a known race-condition NPE bug (AWT-EventQueue-0 NullPointerException)
  when executing inside headless environments lacking a native GUI display.
* Architectural Fixes Applied:
  - Tightened JVM parameters inside 'gradle.properties' to enforce a strict, 
    balanced memory split: 1.5GB max for Gradle ('-Xmx1536m') and 900MB max for 
    the Kotlin Daemon ('kotlin.daemon.jvmopts=-Xmx896m').
  - Set 'org.gradle.workers.max=1' to stop memory-heavy parallel task spikes.
  - Aligned and patched the KSP dependency toolchain inside 'gradle/libs.versions.toml'
    by changing 'googleDevtoolsKsp' from the buggy '2.3.5' release to the stable,
    Kotlin-matched version '2.2.10-2.0.2'.

6. NATIVE ARCHITECTURE UPGRADES & WARNING ELIMINATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Optimization Goal: Update compiler targets natively instead of masking build rules.
* Warning Encountered: 'We recommend using a newer Android Gradle plugin to use compileSdk = 36'.
* Fix Applied: Bypassed the quick-fix warning bypass request, upgraded the 
  Gradle Wrapper directly to '8.11.1', and updated the true Android Gradle Plugin 
  version ('agp') inside 'libs.versions.toml' to '8.9.1' to fully embrace SDK 36.

* Warning Encountered: 'Schema export directory was not provided [...] Room cannot export schema'.
* Fix Applied: Followed the second automation script parameter choice natively; 
  updated line 25 in 'IponDatabase.kt' to explicitly set 'exportSchema = false', 
  successfully cleaning the database configuration log trace.

================================================================================
STATUS: REPOSITORY REPAIRED / DEPENDENCIES ALIGNED / COMPILING SUCCESSFUL
================================================================================
EOF